1
00:00:01,067 --> 00:00:02,200
<i>In Ma'am Rebecca's room,
she has a teddy bear.</i>

2
00:00:02,333 --> 00:00:03,767
<i> Then, there's a spy camera.</i>

3
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:06,800
<i>I'm sure it recorded
what really happened.</i>

4
00:00:06,933 --> 00:00:09,233
<i>Oh, no! I saw it earlier
when I was cleaning.</i>

5
00:00:09,367 --> 00:00:10,833
<i>It was already thrown
in the trash.</i>

6
00:00:10,967 --> 00:00:13,733
<i>Stay here first, okay?
So no one can see you.</i>

7
00:00:13,867 --> 00:00:15,033
<i> I know you need someone.</i>

8
00:00:15,167 --> 00:00:16,700
<i> That's why I'm here.</i>

9
00:00:16,833 --> 00:00:18,500
<i>Just like before,
when something happened to her.</i>

10
00:00:18,633 --> 00:00:19,600
<i> No, you weren't there.</i>

11
00:00:19,733 --> 00:00:20,800
<i> You left.</i>

12
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:23,600
<i>Ma'am, I have something
to tell you.</i>

13
00:00:23,733 --> 00:00:27,800
<i>Just remember,
do not trust Tomas.</i>

14
00:00:27,933 --> 00:00:29,067
<i> Is everything okay?</i>

15
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:32,100
<i>What I was going to say
isn't really important.</i>

16
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:33,567
<i> I'll just say it later.</i>

17
00:00:35,967 --> 00:00:39,933
<i>["NEVER SAY DIE" BY KIM DE LEON
PLAYING]</i>

18
00:00:52,267 --> 00:00:54,000
I know.

19
00:00:54,133 --> 00:00:55,800
I left.

20
00:00:55,933 --> 00:00:57,900
And I shouldn't have.

21
00:00:58,033 --> 00:01:02,200
I was selfish for choosing
to prioritize my career.

22
00:01:02,333 --> 00:01:03,500
When I know
that you're still reeling

23
00:01:03,633 --> 00:01:04,733
from what happened to auntie

24
00:01:04,867 --> 00:01:07,533
even though you were already
making a name for yourself.

25
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:09,300
Don't call it selfishness.

26
00:01:10,567 --> 00:01:12,433
What you did was right.

27
00:01:12,567 --> 00:01:14,033
Because if you stayed

28
00:01:14,167 --> 00:01:17,133
knowing you didn't
really want to,

29
00:01:17,267 --> 00:01:19,067
I would've been hurt even more.

30
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:21,300
But it's okay now.

31
00:01:21,433 --> 00:01:23,267
I understand.

32
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,633
But this time,
I want to do it right, Andrew.

33
00:01:25,767 --> 00:01:26,633
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

34
00:01:26,767 --> 00:01:29,467
I don't want you to be
or feel alone.

35
00:01:29,600 --> 00:01:31,567
I want to be here for you.

36
00:01:33,433 --> 00:01:35,300
So, what's the difference
between<i> afritada</i> and<i> mechado</i> ?

37
00:01:35,433 --> 00:01:37,333
They both have...

38
00:01:37,467 --> 00:01:38,733
- Tomato sauce?
- Joey.

39
00:01:38,867 --> 00:01:40,767
Kyle, Elai.

40
00:01:40,933 --> 00:01:43,433
Hi, Joey.
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

41
00:01:43,567 --> 00:01:46,067
You visited Andrew?

42
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,667
Yes, he still has work.

43
00:01:47,800 --> 00:01:48,933
Yes.

44
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:51,167
Every time you say that to me,

45
00:01:53,433 --> 00:01:56,767
I remember how much I needed you
before.

46
00:01:56,900 --> 00:01:58,500
When something happened
to mommy before,

47
00:01:58,633 --> 00:01:59,967
I kept telling myself...

48
00:02:01,133 --> 00:02:02,133
I could handle it.

49
00:02:04,167 --> 00:02:07,000
I couldn't allow myself
to be hurt. I'm a man, right?

50
00:02:07,133 --> 00:02:08,833
But now,

51
00:02:08,967 --> 00:02:12,467
I don't know if I can accept
that maybe...

52
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:17,067
she might really be gone.

53
00:02:17,200 --> 00:02:18,200
You know...

54
00:02:19,300 --> 00:02:22,233
We really don't know
what lies ahead.

55
00:02:22,367 --> 00:02:24,533
But knowing that there's someone
you can lean on

56
00:02:24,667 --> 00:02:26,733
during hard times like this,

57
00:02:26,867 --> 00:02:28,333
Andrew, I'm sure about that.

58
00:02:29,367 --> 00:02:30,933
I will not leave you.

59
00:02:32,767 --> 00:02:35,033
I'm right here. Never again.

60
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:40,200
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL MUSIC
PLAYING]

61
00:02:40,333 --> 00:02:42,067
Is he still in the garden?

62
00:02:44,333 --> 00:02:46,100
Is he still there?

63
00:02:46,233 --> 00:02:48,767
He went down, I think...

64
00:02:48,933 --> 00:02:51,267
- He went down, right?
- He went down.

65
00:02:51,400 --> 00:02:53,733
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL MUSIC
CONTINUES]

66
00:03:00,633 --> 00:03:02,400
Yeah.

67
00:03:02,533 --> 00:03:03,567
I'll just go to him.

68
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:04,833
Take care.

69
00:03:04,967 --> 00:03:06,033
You too.

70
00:03:07,233 --> 00:03:10,733
[STIRRING EMOTIONAL MUSIC
CONTINUES]

71
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:22,400
She said take care, Ma'am.

72
00:03:22,533 --> 00:03:24,000
We weren't careful.

73
00:03:31,367 --> 00:03:33,133
I already saw him.

74
00:03:33,267 --> 00:03:34,867
I just looked away for a moment,
suddenly he was gone.

75
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:37,267
I didn't see anyone leave, Sir.

76
00:03:37,400 --> 00:03:39,600
I didn't even see anyone
come in.

77
00:03:39,733 --> 00:03:43,133
Could it be that he passed
through the carwash, Sir?

78
00:03:43,267 --> 00:03:44,733
Possible.

79
00:03:44,867 --> 00:03:47,767
But at least now,
we know where to find them.

80
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:50,633
Maybe we don't need
that carwash anymore, Sir.

81
00:03:50,767 --> 00:03:51,633
Looks like we'll get a good tip

82
00:03:51,767 --> 00:03:53,600
from the one
you asked me to find.

83
00:03:53,733 --> 00:03:54,633
I already saw him.

84
00:03:54,800 --> 00:03:56,433
He's on his way here now, Major.

85
00:04:00,400 --> 00:04:03,267
<i>This is really hard
to investigate, Sir.</i>

86
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:05,767
<i> It's been eight years already.</i>

87
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:08,467
<i> I caught a Korean,</i>

88
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:10,533
<i> a syndicate member,</i>

89
00:04:10,667 --> 00:04:11,967
<i> a drug pusher.</i>

90
00:04:13,567 --> 00:04:15,833
<i> He was jailed in Korea too.</i>

91
00:04:15,967 --> 00:04:19,367
<i>When he was released, he set up
operations here in our country.</i>

92
00:04:20,433 --> 00:04:22,300
<i> Could he help us, Major?</i>

93
00:04:22,433 --> 00:04:25,300
<i>This is his social media
account.</i>

94
00:04:25,433 --> 00:04:28,133
<i> His name is Jung Tae-Sik.</i>

95
00:04:30,667 --> 00:04:31,900
Miguel!

96
00:04:36,367 --> 00:04:38,233
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

97
00:04:39,833 --> 00:04:42,300
Bravo, bravo, bravo.

98
00:04:42,433 --> 00:04:46,367
While we're struggling,
you go missing.

99
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:48,067
I thought you wanted
to show off?

100
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:50,800
- What?
- Enough, Matias!

101
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,367
Finish that.

102
00:04:54,500 --> 00:04:56,333
You might be late.

103
00:04:56,467 --> 00:04:57,967
I'll take care of this.

104
00:04:59,300 --> 00:05:00,667
Let's go.

105
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,667
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

106
00:05:15,567 --> 00:05:17,967
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

107
00:05:24,933 --> 00:05:27,133
What's wrong, Joey?
Why are you affected?

108
00:05:28,467 --> 00:05:30,367
Weren't you annoyed with him?

109
00:05:33,067 --> 00:05:35,667
Weren't you fighting?
You disliked him, right?

110
00:05:36,900 --> 00:05:39,100
Why don't you just go back
to those feelings?

111
00:05:42,533 --> 00:05:44,533
Just think you were never close.

112
00:05:48,833 --> 00:05:50,667
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

113
00:05:53,733 --> 00:05:55,467
Just think you never went
through anything together,

114
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:57,900
never shared anything.

115
00:05:58,033 --> 00:06:01,367
<i>They say when you're greeted
by a bright sky,</i>

116
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:05,567
<i>there's a beautiful surprise
waiting for you.</i>

117
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:12,667
Just think you never fell
for him.

118
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:13,967
[SPLASHES]

119
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:21,567
<i> I already love someone else.</i>

120
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:26,933
Why am I being like this?

121
00:06:27,067 --> 00:06:28,800
[SOBBING]

122
00:06:28,933 --> 00:06:30,867
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

123
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:46,333
We had a syndicate
in South Korea before.

124
00:06:46,467 --> 00:06:49,900
Like here in the Philippines,
we also had a rival group.

125
00:06:50,033 --> 00:06:52,767
He was just a teenager
at that time.

126
00:06:52,900 --> 00:06:56,500
But the most frightening thing
about him is...

127
00:06:56,633 --> 00:06:59,800
he wasn't afraid.

128
00:06:59,933 --> 00:07:01,667
Why wasn't he afraid?

129
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:03,900
I'm telling you, Theresa.
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

130
00:07:04,033 --> 00:07:06,200
Pull your investment out now.

131
00:07:07,233 --> 00:07:09,233
And let's go back to Korea,
please...

132
00:07:09,367 --> 00:07:10,333
before I lose control.

133
00:07:10,467 --> 00:07:14,533
Because I swear
I will kill that bastard!

134
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:17,767
I gave you every opportunity

135
00:07:17,900 --> 00:07:19,433
and you wasted all of them.

136
00:07:19,567 --> 00:07:21,900
And now, you want me
to treat you like an equal?

137
00:07:22,033 --> 00:07:23,667
We are equals.

138
00:07:23,800 --> 00:07:25,267
We always were.

139
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,967
But now...

140
00:07:27,100 --> 00:07:29,633
You even talk to me
like I work for you.

141
00:07:31,067 --> 00:07:34,400
This is not Korea.

142
00:07:36,233 --> 00:07:38,633
Here, respect is earned.

143
00:07:38,767 --> 00:07:42,633
He could fight and keep on
with the older ones.

144
00:07:42,767 --> 00:07:45,167
And while things were chaotic,

145
00:07:45,300 --> 00:07:47,967
even if it was just
a simple strike

146
00:07:48,133 --> 00:07:49,733
with a blunt object

147
00:07:49,867 --> 00:07:52,200
or a blow to the head,

148
00:07:52,333 --> 00:07:56,033
he never hesitates.

149
00:07:56,167 --> 00:08:00,033
That means he was exposed
to violence early.

150
00:08:00,167 --> 00:08:01,067
Exactly.

151
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:04,167
He was different
when he took a hit.

152
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:08,700
That's why when I received
the photograph you sent,

153
00:08:08,833 --> 00:08:13,867
there was no doubt,
I recognized him immediately.

154
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,767
He's that kid.

155
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:18,067
He's that boy.

156
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:19,233
I've told you many times

157
00:08:19,367 --> 00:08:21,233
on exactly how you can
put yourself

158
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:23,000
in Berdugo's radar,
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

159
00:08:23,133 --> 00:08:25,233
and you ignored
every single one.

160
00:08:25,367 --> 00:08:27,400
So if you can't prove yourself,

161
00:08:27,533 --> 00:08:30,933
then yes, you can go back
to Korea.

162
00:08:31,067 --> 00:08:34,067
Dead or alive,

163
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:35,967
it won't matter to me.

164
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:38,333
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

165
00:08:51,233 --> 00:08:53,167
If he's been in the syndicate

166
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:55,500
since he was young,
like you said,

167
00:08:55,667 --> 00:08:58,900
so why doesn't his name appear
in our files?

168
00:09:00,333 --> 00:09:03,433
Could it be that his name
is different?

169
00:09:03,567 --> 00:09:04,967
His name is not real.

170
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:06,333
It's a fake name.

171
00:09:07,633 --> 00:09:09,567
What's his name?

172
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:11,333
Kang Dae-Hyun.

173
00:09:16,167 --> 00:09:17,733
This is him.

174
00:09:17,867 --> 00:09:19,233
But it's written in Korean.

175
00:09:19,367 --> 00:09:21,400
Can you translate?

176
00:09:21,533 --> 00:09:23,533
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

177
00:09:29,633 --> 00:09:33,300
“Drug suspect gone missing
after police raid”

178
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,667
<i> Sir, Sir Andrew.</i>

179
00:09:42,567 --> 00:09:44,267
Miss Clarissa...

180
00:09:46,967 --> 00:09:50,933
Thank you so much
for visiting mommy.

181
00:09:51,067 --> 00:09:53,067
I'm sure she appreciates it.

182
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,800
I know she's happy
that you're here.

183
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:58,833
Where's Joey?

184
00:09:58,967 --> 00:10:01,700
You haven't seen each other yet?

185
00:10:01,867 --> 00:10:03,600
You haven't talked yet?

186
00:10:03,733 --> 00:10:06,100
She went to see you
in the garden.

187
00:10:06,233 --> 00:10:08,000
I didn't see her there.

188
00:10:08,133 --> 00:10:10,100
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:10:10,233 --> 00:10:12,900
Okay, I'll just go back
to her there.

190
00:10:13,033 --> 00:10:14,533
No need.

191
00:10:14,667 --> 00:10:17,033
I'll just call her.

192
00:10:17,167 --> 00:10:19,133
I'll just tell her you're here.

193
00:10:20,433 --> 00:10:22,000
Excuse me.

194
00:10:22,133 --> 00:10:24,167
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

195
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:35,700
[PHONE RINGING]

196
00:10:35,867 --> 00:10:38,733
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES♪]

197
00:10:51,433 --> 00:10:52,867
Mom?

198
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:54,567
Joey...

199
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:55,600
where are you?

200
00:10:55,733 --> 00:10:58,133
<i> Sir Andrew is here.</i>

201
00:10:58,267 --> 00:11:00,533
He said you didn't get to talk.

202
00:11:00,667 --> 00:11:02,433
What happened?

203
00:11:02,567 --> 00:11:05,433
I didn't catch him, Mom.

204
00:11:05,567 --> 00:11:08,167
Why? Where did you go?

205
00:11:08,333 --> 00:11:09,533
I just went out
for a while, Mom,

206
00:11:09,667 --> 00:11:11,167
because I needed
to buy something,

207
00:11:11,300 --> 00:11:12,867
but I'll come back right away.

208
00:11:13,967 --> 00:11:15,000
Okay.

209
00:11:15,133 --> 00:11:17,267
Be careful.

210
00:11:17,400 --> 00:11:18,700
Okay, Mom.

211
00:11:19,833 --> 00:11:21,767
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

212
00:11:33,067 --> 00:11:34,967
You're okay now, Joey.

213
00:11:35,100 --> 00:11:36,567
You're okay now.

214
00:11:38,067 --> 00:11:41,100
Don't you have more things
to worry about than that?

215
00:11:44,133 --> 00:11:45,667
You're okay now.

216
00:11:49,967 --> 00:11:51,433
[PHONE CHIMES]

217
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:57,533
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

218
00:12:01,233 --> 00:12:02,367
What?

219
00:12:03,433 --> 00:12:06,467
[PHONE RINGS]

220
00:12:09,233 --> 00:12:10,333
<i> Hello, Joey?</i>

221
00:12:12,367 --> 00:12:13,467
Jin Ho?

222
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:17,533
I knew it.

223
00:12:17,667 --> 00:12:19,400
That's why I was restless.

224
00:12:19,533 --> 00:12:21,633
That damn Jin Ho.
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:12:21,767 --> 00:12:25,567
Does this mean he's connected
to Berdugo's group?

226
00:12:25,700 --> 00:12:29,067
We don't know if he's an ally
or an enemy.

227
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:31,333
But I'm sure he's not a cop.

228
00:12:31,467 --> 00:12:33,700
He's part of a syndicate.

229
00:12:33,833 --> 00:12:37,400
We'll use him
to get closer to Berdugo.

230
00:12:38,133 --> 00:12:40,900
Make an initial report for chief

231
00:12:41,033 --> 00:12:43,233
so this surveillance
becomes official.

232
00:12:43,367 --> 00:12:45,200
Yes, Major.

233
00:12:45,333 --> 00:12:48,567
But didn't you mention
he's a friend of your daughter,

234
00:12:48,733 --> 00:12:49,800
Joey?

235
00:12:55,767 --> 00:12:57,033
[LIGHT AMBIENT MUSIC PLAYING]

236
00:12:57,167 --> 00:12:59,733
[PHONE RINGING]

237
00:13:03,733 --> 00:13:05,200
Dad, there's...

238
00:13:05,333 --> 00:13:07,800
Joey, listen carefully.

239
00:13:07,933 --> 00:13:10,267
This is about your friend,
Jin Ho.

240
00:13:10,400 --> 00:13:11,300
What?

241
00:13:11,433 --> 00:13:13,400
He's not really
a Korean police officer.

242
00:13:13,533 --> 00:13:14,967
<i>He's a criminal.
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

243
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:16,733
What did you say, Dad?

244
00:13:16,867 --> 00:13:18,567
Where did you get that?

245
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:20,900
Joey, I have evidence.

246
00:13:21,033 --> 00:13:22,867
He's a syndicate member.

247
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,067
<i> That means...</i>

248
00:13:25,200 --> 00:13:27,300
he cannot be trusted.

249
00:13:27,433 --> 00:13:29,333
Don't go with him.

250
00:13:29,467 --> 00:13:31,533
[UNEASY MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

251
00:13:47,500 --> 00:13:49,000
Did you hear what I said?

252
00:13:50,967 --> 00:13:52,633
Dad, let's just talk later.

253
00:13:52,767 --> 00:13:54,133
Okay.

254
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:55,133
Joey!

255
00:13:55,267 --> 00:13:56,800
Joey...

256
00:13:57,967 --> 00:14:01,933
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING♪]

257
00:14:02,067 --> 00:14:04,800
How are you?
Where have you been?

258
00:14:04,933 --> 00:14:06,600
You owe us a lot of stories.

259
00:14:06,733 --> 00:14:09,467
We don't know
what happened to you.

260
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,767
Joey, how are you?

261
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:14,300
I'm so glad that you're here.

262
00:14:14,433 --> 00:14:16,033
I missed you...
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

263
00:14:16,167 --> 00:14:19,067
and the guys, you know.

264
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:21,933
And I'm sorry
if I haven't been in touch,

265
00:14:22,067 --> 00:14:24,600
and I know that I have a lot
of explaining to do.

266
00:14:26,033 --> 00:14:28,367
Yeah, we don't know
what happened to you.

267
00:14:28,533 --> 00:14:30,967
We were worried about you.

268
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:33,500
We? Wait...

269
00:14:33,633 --> 00:14:35,500
Are the guys here too? Where?

270
00:14:35,633 --> 00:14:37,700
No, it's just me today.

271
00:14:37,833 --> 00:14:39,433
Okay.

272
00:14:39,567 --> 00:14:41,300
You know,
it would have been nice

273
00:14:41,433 --> 00:14:42,700
to have a little reunion.

274
00:14:42,833 --> 00:14:46,600
All of us together,
just like before.

275
00:14:47,533 --> 00:14:48,700
Yeah.

276
00:14:48,833 --> 00:14:52,200
We thought you went to Korea
without saying goodbye first.

277
00:14:53,333 --> 00:14:54,733
I never left.

278
00:14:54,867 --> 00:14:56,233
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

279
00:14:56,367 --> 00:14:58,900
But let's not talk
about me today.

280
00:14:59,033 --> 00:15:01,200
What about you? How are you?

281
00:15:01,367 --> 00:15:02,600
How's Peter?

282
00:15:02,733 --> 00:15:05,600
And what about your Boss Idol,
Andrew?

283
00:15:05,733 --> 00:15:07,300
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

284
00:15:08,867 --> 00:15:11,500
So, I started investigating
mom's case.

285
00:15:12,933 --> 00:15:15,800
So, it's either the medicine
she took was expired,

286
00:15:15,933 --> 00:15:17,500
which it wasn't,

287
00:15:17,633 --> 00:15:21,067
or the dose was just too much.

288
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:24,433
Maybe there were other medicines
that shouldn't be taken together

289
00:15:24,567 --> 00:15:26,633
because, if that happens,
there are side effects?

290
00:15:28,633 --> 00:15:30,667
I asked the doctor.
She said there was none.

291
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:32,967
So, it's either Aunt Rebecca
didn't notice

292
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:35,733
that she took too much medicine

293
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:38,100
or she did it on purpose?

294
00:15:38,233 --> 00:15:39,533
Hey, no way.

295
00:15:39,667 --> 00:15:41,167
Why? I'm just saying.

296
00:15:42,433 --> 00:15:43,367
Boss, sorry, okay?

297
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:45,733
I didn't mean anything bad.

298
00:15:45,867 --> 00:15:47,300
I know mommy.

299
00:15:48,433 --> 00:15:51,267
I know she would never do that.

300
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:54,000
I know her as a fighter,
not a quitter.

301
00:15:55,033 --> 00:15:56,867
And it's not like someone
did that in your house, right?

302
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,600
That seems impossible.

303
00:15:58,733 --> 00:16:01,833
You can trust the people
in your house, right?

304
00:16:01,967 --> 00:16:05,033
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

305
00:16:07,167 --> 00:16:09,900
Oh, why did you go quiet?

306
00:16:10,067 --> 00:16:11,800
Is there something wrong?

307
00:16:11,933 --> 00:16:13,800
How's mom?

308
00:16:13,933 --> 00:16:15,233
They said her room
is being prepared

309
00:16:15,367 --> 00:16:17,267
so she can be transferred
from the ICU.

310
00:16:18,533 --> 00:16:20,033
She's out of danger.

311
00:16:20,167 --> 00:16:22,400
Really? That's good news.

312
00:16:23,167 --> 00:16:25,000
Well, not quite, Yvette.

313
00:16:25,133 --> 00:16:27,000
She still hasn't woken up.

314
00:16:27,133 --> 00:16:29,067
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

315
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:35,933
Andrew's a bit busy.

316
00:16:36,067 --> 00:16:37,500
You, how are you?

317
00:16:37,633 --> 00:16:39,567
Did you catch Theresa?

318
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:43,467
Yeah, you can say that.

319
00:16:43,633 --> 00:16:48,133
Oh, so you got a new assignment?

320
00:16:48,267 --> 00:16:49,600
You guessed it right,

321
00:16:49,733 --> 00:16:53,633
but I can't tell you
the details.

322
00:16:53,767 --> 00:16:56,633
Wow, keeping secrets from me.

323
00:16:56,767 --> 00:16:58,167
You don't have to do that.

324
00:16:58,300 --> 00:17:00,367
What? Not even a little
information? Nothing?

325
00:17:03,200 --> 00:17:04,600
Okay.

326
00:17:04,733 --> 00:17:06,567
So, here's the truth.

327
00:17:06,700 --> 00:17:08,500
You know, yes, I've been busy

328
00:17:08,633 --> 00:17:10,267
because I'm working
on something new.

329
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:11,733
That's why I haven't
had the chance

330
00:17:11,867 --> 00:17:14,333
to check on all of you.

331
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:16,033
What is it?

332
00:17:16,167 --> 00:17:17,300
You can tell me.

333
00:17:17,433 --> 00:17:18,500
You can trust me.

334
00:17:18,633 --> 00:17:20,100
I mean...
[GRUNTS SOFTLY]

335
00:17:20,233 --> 00:17:22,267
[PHONE CHIMES]

336
00:17:22,400 --> 00:17:23,767
Wait.

337
00:17:23,900 --> 00:17:25,333
Sorry.

338
00:17:25,467 --> 00:17:28,100
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

339
00:17:28,233 --> 00:17:30,200
Joey...

340
00:17:31,433 --> 00:17:32,633
I have to go.

341
00:17:32,767 --> 00:17:33,900
Already?

342
00:17:34,033 --> 00:17:35,133
Yeah, I know, but...

343
00:17:35,267 --> 00:17:36,867
Duty calls.

344
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,067
But I promise
to make it up to you soon.

345
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:41,333
Maybe the guys
could join us too.

346
00:17:41,467 --> 00:17:44,333
But now, I really have to go.

347
00:17:45,533 --> 00:17:46,833
Okay.

348
00:17:46,967 --> 00:17:49,267
It's really nice
to see you again, Joey.

349
00:17:50,367 --> 00:17:53,067
Yeah, take care.

350
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,900
- See you.
- See you.

351
00:17:55,033 --> 00:17:56,367
Bye.

352
00:17:56,500 --> 00:17:59,400
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

353
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,000
Thanks, Doc.

354
00:18:07,133 --> 00:18:09,000
Okay, I'll leave you for now.

355
00:18:11,700 --> 00:18:13,833
Ma'am...

356
00:18:13,967 --> 00:18:15,567
do you have anything else
you want me to do?

357
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:17,533
I just need to do something.

358
00:18:17,667 --> 00:18:18,633
Nothing more.

359
00:18:18,767 --> 00:18:19,933
Okay, thank you.

360
00:18:20,067 --> 00:18:21,200
Yes.

361
00:18:21,333 --> 00:18:23,733
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

362
00:18:31,900 --> 00:18:33,167
What's wrong, Andrew?

363
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:37,167
Yvette, I still can't figure out
how this happened to mommy.

364
00:18:37,300 --> 00:18:38,233
Yvette, I know in my heart

365
00:18:38,367 --> 00:18:40,733
that she could never do this
to herself.

366
00:18:40,867 --> 00:18:43,633
So, who? Who would do this?

367
00:18:43,767 --> 00:18:46,167
I know everyone
who comes close to mommy.

368
00:18:47,633 --> 00:18:51,167
If someone was at fault,

369
00:18:51,300 --> 00:18:54,100
I'm sure it wasn't done
intentionally, Andrew.

370
00:18:54,233 --> 00:18:55,800
Right, Hon?

371
00:18:55,967 --> 00:18:58,000
We will never know
until she wakes up.

372
00:18:59,067 --> 00:19:00,500
Right now, what's important

373
00:19:00,633 --> 00:19:03,600
is our prayers
that she gets through this.

374
00:19:03,733 --> 00:19:04,867
And us...

375
00:19:06,433 --> 00:19:08,000
we should stay strong for her.

376
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:11,300
That's right.

377
00:19:11,433 --> 00:19:15,033
So, stop asking questions
like that, Andrew, okay?

378
00:19:15,167 --> 00:19:18,133
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

379
00:19:28,600 --> 00:19:30,367
Who should I believe?

380
00:19:32,467 --> 00:19:34,833
Dad wouldn't lie to me.

381
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:39,600
Maybe his intel was just wrong.

382
00:19:39,733 --> 00:19:41,200
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

383
00:19:41,333 --> 00:19:45,233
But Jin Ho has a secret
he doesn't want to tell me.

384
00:19:45,367 --> 00:19:47,167
Who should I believe?

385
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:49,633
It's hard...

386
00:19:50,833 --> 00:19:53,033
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

387
00:19:53,167 --> 00:19:54,867
Hello?

388
00:19:55,833 --> 00:19:57,733
Okay, let's just talk later.

389
00:19:57,867 --> 00:20:00,333
Okay. Bye, bye.

390
00:20:03,933 --> 00:20:06,233
It's hard not having someone
to talk to.

391
00:20:06,367 --> 00:20:09,300
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

392
00:20:16,067 --> 00:20:18,033
[SOFT UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING]

393
00:20:35,533 --> 00:20:36,933
Boss Idol.

394
00:20:38,633 --> 00:20:39,933
Miss Clarissa.

395
00:20:40,067 --> 00:20:41,767
I've already prepared dinner.

396
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:43,467
Will you be having dinner here?

397
00:20:44,533 --> 00:20:46,233
No. How about you?

398
00:20:46,367 --> 00:20:48,433
I'll just eat at home.

399
00:20:48,567 --> 00:20:50,000
I'll go ahead.

400
00:20:50,133 --> 00:20:51,533
Oh, about Joey...

401
00:20:52,567 --> 00:20:53,967
How is she?

402
00:20:54,100 --> 00:20:55,867
She's okay.

403
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:58,133
You still haven't talked?

404
00:20:58,267 --> 00:20:59,567
Not yet.

405
00:20:59,700 --> 00:21:01,267
Just call her.

406
00:21:02,967 --> 00:21:04,067
I'll go ahead.

407
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:06,133
Take care, okay?

408
00:21:06,267 --> 00:21:08,833
[DREAMY MUSIC PLAYING]

409
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:21,833
[DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

410
00:21:30,033 --> 00:21:33,000
[DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

411
00:21:38,367 --> 00:21:40,067
- Hi!
- Hi.

412
00:21:40,200 --> 00:21:41,633
Missed me?

413
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:44,833
[DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

414
00:21:48,733 --> 00:21:51,667
It's really hard to believe,
Dad.

415
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:53,467
Can your source
really be trusted

416
00:21:53,600 --> 00:21:55,567
about what they're saying
about Jin Ho?

417
00:21:55,700 --> 00:21:57,867
Maybe it's just fake news.

418
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,700
His name isn't even Jin Ho.

419
00:21:59,833 --> 00:22:01,867
It's Kang Dae-Hyun.

420
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,467
And how many times
do I have to tell you?

421
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:05,633
That's what was reported to us.

422
00:22:05,767 --> 00:22:07,700
Why don't you believe it?

423
00:22:08,833 --> 00:22:12,000
Because, Dad, even if that man
is cranky, I trust him

424
00:22:12,133 --> 00:22:15,600
because he's saved my life
several times.

425
00:22:15,767 --> 00:22:17,967
I thought maybe...

426
00:22:18,100 --> 00:22:20,400
he's undercover for a mission.

427
00:22:20,533 --> 00:22:25,167
And they just suspected
he was part of the syndicate?

428
00:22:25,300 --> 00:22:26,733
But what if it's true?

429
00:22:26,867 --> 00:22:29,267
I suspect it's connected
to the syndicate

430
00:22:29,400 --> 00:22:31,000
here in the Philippines.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

431
00:22:31,133 --> 00:22:35,600
Maybe he's a supplier or buyer
of those coming from Korea.

432
00:22:35,733 --> 00:22:38,833
I think he knows Berdugo.

433
00:22:38,967 --> 00:22:41,667
How can we find that out?

434
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:43,800
What if we confront him?

435
00:22:43,933 --> 00:22:46,000
- I'll call him.
- Wait, don't.

436
00:22:46,133 --> 00:22:48,000
I thought of another way.

437
00:22:48,133 --> 00:22:50,400
And no one else should know
about this,

438
00:22:50,567 --> 00:22:52,400
not even Andrew.

439
00:22:52,533 --> 00:22:55,200
Because he might report it
on Tirada,

440
00:22:55,333 --> 00:22:57,000
and the syndicate
might find out.

441
00:22:58,100 --> 00:23:01,200
[PHONE RINGING]
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

442
00:23:04,767 --> 00:23:05,800
Hello?

443
00:23:05,933 --> 00:23:08,900
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

444
00:23:11,367 --> 00:23:14,333
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

445
00:23:19,100 --> 00:23:21,267
I also want to meet the one
you brought into our group.

446
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:24,300
Matias said he doesn't trust
that man.

447
00:23:24,467 --> 00:23:26,567
<i>That Matias doesn't trust
anyone.</i>

448
00:23:26,700 --> 00:23:28,467
Are you sure that's the Korean
we're looking for?

449
00:23:28,600 --> 00:23:29,567
I'll go with you.

450
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:30,833
I really just want to see

451
00:23:30,967 --> 00:23:32,600
if what you're saying
about Jin Ho is true,

452
00:23:32,733 --> 00:23:35,033
that he's a criminal
and part of Berdugo's syndicate.

453
00:23:35,167 --> 00:23:36,100
Who is he talking to?

454
00:23:36,233 --> 00:23:37,100
Let's follow him.

455
00:23:37,233 --> 00:23:38,533
Who were here the other day?

456
00:23:38,667 --> 00:23:40,467
It was me, Ma'am Clarissa,

457
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:42,667
the kids, Ma'am Yvette,

458
00:23:42,800 --> 00:23:43,900
and Sir Tomas.

459
00:23:44,033 --> 00:23:46,767
It's broken. I'm sorry.

460
00:23:46,900 --> 00:23:47,700
Let me see.

461
00:23:47,833 --> 00:23:50,100
I got this from inside.

462
00:23:50,233 --> 00:23:52,267
Looks like a camera.
